<section class="sec soft"><div class="wrap split"><div><div class="eyebrow">The fellowship</div><h2 class="" data-bn="ছয় মাস, পাঁচ ধাপ।">Six months, five stages.</h2></div>
<ol class="tl rv"><li class="now"><small>Month 1</small><h3>Discover</h3><p class="hint">Sharpen the problem with a mentor and the people who live with it.</p></li>
<li><small>Months 2–3</small><h3>Develop</h3><p class="hint">Build a working prototype with lab access and a small grant.</p></li>
<li><small>Months 4–5</small><h3>Validate</h3><p class="hint">Field test and independent review.</p></li>
<li><small>Month 6</small><h3>Brief</h3><p class="hint">Present the evidence at Demo Day and in a policy brief.</p></li>
<li><small>After</small><h3>Implement</h3><p class="hint">Pilots, adoption or a venture with partners, with your credit and stake agreed in writing.</p></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="sec"><div class="wrap split"><div><div class="eyebrow">Questions</div><h2 class="" data-bn="আবেদনের আগে">Before you apply</h2></div>
<div class="faq rv"><details><summary>Who can apply?</summary><p>Students, recent graduates and early-career researchers and engineers in Bangladesh. You need an idea on the Idea Ledger to apply for a Delta Fellowship; other roles do not require one.</p></details><details><summary>Is it paid?</summary><p>Delta Fellows receive a development grant during the fellowship. Amounts will be published with each open call. Mentor and reviewer roles are voluntary.</p></details><details><summary>Do I keep my idea?</summary><p>Yes. Credit stays with you at every stage. Any equity or benefit-sharing is agreed in writing before a venture or pilot starts.</p></details><details><summary>Can I apply in Bangla?</summary><p>Yes. Applications, interviews and reviews can be in Bangla or English.</p></details><details><summary>When is the next call?</summary><p>The first open call is planned for the launch phase. Subscribe to the Delta Dispatch to hear first.</p></details></div></div></section>
